# Rooms config. rooms/install.sh copies this to ~/.config/agent-rooms/config.env (or $AGENT_ROOMS_CONFIG).
# Read by roomd.py, roomctl and room_mcp.py. Real environment variables win.
# KEY=VALUE, one per line; a leading ~ and $HOME are expanded. Every key is optional: the value shown is the default.

# --- Rooms server (roomd.py) ---
# AGENT_ROOMS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3396         where roomctl and the room MCP reach the server
# AGENT_ROOMS_PORT=3396
# AGENT_ROOMS_HOST=127.0.0.1                    0.0.0.0 to reach it from other devices, then add only those devices to ALLOW
# AGENT_ROOMS_ALLOW=127.0.0.0/8,::1/128         client networks it answers; Tailscale: your devices' 100.x.y.z/32 (narrower than 100.64.0.0/10)
# AGENT_ROOMS_HOSTNAMES=                       extra names requests may be addressed to (comma separated); this
#                                               machine's hostname and its Tailscale name are always accepted
# AGENT_ROOMS_DIR=~/.local/share/agent-rooms/rooms
# AGENT_ROOMS_HUMAN=Human                       the name the web page posts as (you)
# AGENT_ROOMS_AGENT_SEND=                       optional: a command `<cmd> <agent id> <text>` that types an @mention
#                                               into a live interactive agent session (empty = chat only). It gets
#                                               untrusted multi-line text: it must not interpret it
